## Restart operating rules

1. The Astra parent performs planning, target decisions, arithmetic, artifact writing, and acceptance sequentially.
2. Use zero workers while developing the target and the first complete formula. Once a complete draft exists, at most one read-only native reviewer may be useful. Its prompt must explicitly forbid spawning children, edits, unrelated searches, or repeating the full research task. If pending worker state is unresolved, review locally.
3. Use only OpenAI-native reasoning and delegation. Historical external-provider routes do not belong to this restart.
4. Reuse exact local source locations and verified observations from the abandoned pass. Recheck facts that can change, especially stock authority, without repeating a whole-repository census.
5. Read one bounded topic per output. Return selected fields and line references; do not combine several large full-file reads. Target approximately 2,000 output tokens per investigative call, except a required complete instruction document or the final formatter report.
6. Maintain a decision ledger: decision, supporting source, uncertainty, and which artifact changes. A new search must resolve a named open decision.
7. A scientific uncertainty affects its implicated stock, model, claim, or card. It must not become an endless prerequisite for drafting the complete development formula.
8. Use one existing Python environment and one import check from this worktree. Do not reinstall environments or repair shared infrastructure within this studio task.
9. Run focused formula checks and one initial integrated screen. Rerun only after a concrete correction or to verify final bytes. Do not tune the engine, family thresholds, or authority pins to obtain a pass.
10. Preserve original artifacts and failed diagnostic receipts. No shared engine/backend/governance edits, new pipeline scripts, commits, merges, pushes, purchases, or physical compounding.

